en:
My name is Akemi Iwashita.
I'm a third-year.
So I'm the one telling the second story.{p}

He hurriedly shoved his hand inside his desk, but what he was looking for wasn't there either.
"Oh no!
My art supplies are all in the art room!"{p}

...Heh heh heh.
He really was a forgetful one, wasn't he?
He had even forgotten where his own things were.{p}

Heh heh heh...
Don't worry.
I'll keep it a secret for you.{p}

Nanase screamed and ran.
Back the way he came, toward the new school building.
Then the soldier came after Nanase, clanking and rumbling.{p}

That's right.
You got it.
Nanase ducked into the nearest classroom and decided to hide, keeping still under a desk.{p}

What Nanase saw was the terrifying face of the soldier, peering in at him...☆
The soldier twisted his lips into an eerie grin.
"So this is where you were..."{p}

But by the time the teacher on night duty heard the scream and came running, there was no one to be seen in the classroom.
Neither Nanase nor the soldier was there.
All anyone could hear, they say, was a faint, dull clanking coming from the direction of the walkway...{p}

Nanase...?
Or someone from much longer ago...?
Heh heh, maybe it wasn't only corpses that cart carried.{p}

"Say, {a}.
Would you take everyone and head back to the club room ahead of me?"
"Is something wrong?"{p}

Heh heh heh...
Of course not.
If you gave up on your homework here, everyone would laugh at you.{p}

You'd go back for it?
Yes, I think that's much better.
Better than giving up on your homework, at least...{p}

Heh heh, to tell you the truth...
I...
I was sure you'd answer that way.{p}

Still half asleep, Nanase did as his mother told him and headed for school in a daze.
Come to think of it, what time is it now...?
...That's what he was wondering.{p}

Heh heh heh...
Don't worry.
I'll keep it a secret for you.{p}

The old school building is off-limits now, but back then, classes were still held there.
Mostly lessons that used the special rooms, like art and music.
...Shall we go on with the story?{p}

...This is strange.
Something's wrong...
There was something he just couldn't make sense of, and he couldn't bring himself to open the door.{p}

Students soaked to the skin...
Students covered in mud...
Every face was pale, without the slightest trace of life.{p}

Heh heh heh...
Still studying even after death... ghosts have it rough, don't they?
But a living person who wanders in there has it even rougher.{p}

"Come on, let go!
Let me gooo☆"
And just like that, his consciousness slipped away......{p}

Someone who happened to be passing by had found Nanase collapsed at the school gate and taken him to the hospital.
He... wasn't especially badly hurt, but for a while, apparently, he was in a state of suspended animation...
Right around the time his mother heard his voice.{p}

When he stole a look inside through the window, everyone was listening intently to a lesson.
...Looks like there's a class going on.
What kind of class could they be having at this hour?{p}

Heh heh...
He was frozen stiff with fear, you see.
Though he insists he was just watching to see what would happen.{p}

I see...
So you're the type whose body moves before you think, {a}.
Nanase was the same.{p}

"Wh-whoaaa!"
His legs nearly gave out, but Nanase desperately got to his feet and started running again.
And then the soldier came after him, clattering and clunking all the way.{p}

...{a}?
Do you seriously think that?
Do you really think anyone would charge at a ghost, just because they can't get away?{p}

...I see.
You don't want to go that badly.
Oh well, it can't be helped.{p}

With those words, Iwashita disappeared into the darkness at the far end of the hallway.
"Well then, everyone, shall we go back to the club room?"
We left the old school building, leaving Iwashita behind.{p}

"It can't be...☆"
Everyone broke into a run at once.
Toward the old school building, where the voice had come from...{p}

That's cruel...
"It's dangerous to leave a girl alone!"
...That's what they were all saying, and yet.{p}
